PASS L1 B is real antisymmetric (h = iB hermitian, odd symbol)
PASS L2 eps B eps = -B  (Theta_M = eps K is a symmetry of h = iB)
PASS L3 shift S_mu (zeta_mu = (-1)^(x_{>mu})) commutes with B, mu=1,2,3
PASS L3c control: zeta_mu = eta_mu does NOT commute with B for some mu
PASS L4 S_mu S_nu = - S_nu S_mu (mu != nu)
PASS L5 S_mu^2 = translation by 2 e_mu
PASS L6 P_stag: xi(x)->eps(x) xi(-x) commutes with B
PASS L7 eps S_mu eps = -S_mu
PASS F1 lattice B reduces on 2-periodic envelopes to sum_j (q_j-1/q_j) G_j, G_j=eta_j T_j (all 64 q; affine in the three coefficients, so all q)
PASS F2 lattice shift S_mu reduces to q_mu * S0_mu on the fibre (all 64 q)
PASS F3 P_stag maps fibre(q)->fibre(1/q) with u -> eps u (all 64 q)
PASS F4 Theta_M = eps K maps fibre(q)->fibre(1/q) with u -> eps conj(u) (all 64 q)
PASS A1 G_j real symmetric involutions, pairwise anticommuting (Dirac matrices of h(k) = -sum sin k_j G_j)
PASS A2 S0_mu real symmetric involutions, pairwise anticommuting, commuting with every G_j
PASS A3 eps anticommutes with every G_j and every S0_mu
PASS A4 chirality Sigma = -i G1G2G3: hermitian, Sigma^2=1, purely imaginary, commutes with all G_j (hence with h(k) for every k), traceless
PASS A5 eps Sigma eps = - Sigma  (site parity eps exchanges the two chiralities)
PASS A6 Sigma commutes with every S0_mu (shifts do not exchange chiralities)
PASS A7 central shift element Z_S=S1S2S3 equals c*Sigma with c=-1j (so chirality = eigenvalue of the central shift element)
PASS A8 h(q): P h(q) P^-1 = h(1/q) and Theta_M h(q) Theta_M^-1 = h(1/q) on the fibre (all 64 q)
PASS A9 Theta_M preserves chirality: eps conj(Sigma) eps = +Sigma;  P_stag flips it: eps Sigma eps = -Sigma
PASS A10 taste generators T_mu = S0_mu Sigma: involutions, pairwise anticommuting, commute with G_j and Sigma
PASS A11 eps T_mu eps = +T_mu (P_stag trivial on T-taste);  Theta_M: eps conj(T_mu) eps = -T_mu (antiunitary, flips all three taste Paulis)
PASS B1 four blocks (Sigma, T_3) = (+-,+-): orthogonal projectors, trace 2 each, sum = identity
PASS B2 action on block labels (sigma=chirality, tau=taste): S1,S2,Theta flip tau and keep sigma; S3 keeps both; P_stag flips sigma and keeps tau
PASS B3 group generated by {S_mu, P_stag, Theta_M} acts transitively on the 4 blocks (orbit size 4)
PASS B4 only P_stag changes sigma: every word fixing a block has an even number of P_stag factors (so a chiral block's stabiliser contains no chirality-exchanging element)
PASS W1 on the Sigma=+1 block h(k)^2 = |sin k|^2 (massless Weyl dispersion, two 2-component Weyl fermions per fibre = 4 complex components)
PASS W2 mass space {M : M G_j + G_j M = 0 for all j} has dimension 8 (= eps x taste-Pauli algebra)
PASS W3 every gap-opening bilinear mass anticommutes with Sigma: its block-diagonal part vanishes, it couples Sigma=+1 to Sigma=-1 only (a single chirality block carries no bilinear mass, with or without Theta_M, P_stag)
PASS W4 free propagator identity P (Pi_L G(z,q) Pi_L) P^-1 = Pi_R G(z,1/q) Pi_R at 4 momenta, exact: L and R spectral content are exchanged by P_stag
PASS C1 binary quaternion group Q8 inside SU(2) generated exactly (order 8)
PASS C2 Frobenius-Schur indicator of the SU(2) doublet restricted to Q8 = -1 (pseudoreal)
PASS C3 real commutant of one doublet (real dim 4) is 4-dim, of two doublets 16-dim (H and M_2(H))
PASS C4 generic element of the one-doublet commutant has det = (positive-definite quadratic form)^2: division algebra, so the 4-dim real rep is irreducible (no invariant real 2-plane, hence no Majorana half of one doublet)
PASS C5 two doublets: the diagonal real 4-plane {(v,v)} is G-invariant (rank test): halving a pair leaves one ordinary doublet, no net gain
PASS C6 Frobenius-Schur: U(1) charge 1 (via Z_4) = 0 (complex);  SO(3) triplet (24 cube rotations) = 1 (real);  SU(3) triplet on its centre Z_3 = 0 (complex)
PASS C7 count: complex staggered field = 8 complex fibre comps = 2 Dirac = 4 Weyl; reduced (Majorana) field = 8 real comps = 1 Dirac = 2 Weyl = 2 Majorana-Weyl
PASS C8 three right-handed neutrino labels: reduced fields give Majorana-Weyl labels in pairs, so 3 labels need 2 reduced fields = 4 labels (one surplus sterile Weyl); no 3-Majorana-per-field identification exists
PASS C9 (complex staggered fields only) content n x (SM+nu_R) + m x mirror matches iff n = m even; n = 3 impossible, smallest n >= 3 is 4 (checked n,m <= 8: [(2, 2), (4, 4), (6, 6), (8, 8)])
PASS Q1 8 Majoranas on 4 qubits: Clifford relations
PASS Q2 Omega hermitian; characteristic polynomial (x+14) x^8 (x-2)^7: unique ground state, gap 14W for W>0
PASS Q3 control: flipping one coefficient sign changes the spectrum (no unique gap 14)
PASS Q4 antiunitary T=UK fixing every gamma: T^2 and T P T^-1 = (+-)P give the Fidkowski-Kitaev pattern nu=2:(+,-) 4:(-,+) 6:(-,-) 8:(+,+) (exact matrices)
PASS Q5 T-symmetric parity-even hermitian operators: nu=4 -> only {1, P} (2 operators) so every T-symmetric H on 4 Majoranas has spectrum c + dP, doubly degenerate (T^2=-1 Kramers); nu=8 -> 72 operators (1+70+1)
PASS Q6 all 28 hermitian bilinears i g_a g_b are T-odd on the 8-Majorana carrier (exact)
PASS D1 decoupled clusters (t=0): spectrum of Omega_1+Omega_2 is -28 (x1), -14 (x16), ... : unique ground state, gap 14 (exact sums of the single-cluster spectrum)
PASS D2 inter-cluster hop V = i sum_a g_a(1) g_a(2) has operator norm 8.000000 <= 8
PASS D3 dimer of clusters (checked numerically, 256x256): ground state unique with gap >= 14W - 2t||V|| for W=10,3 (t=1); (W,t,gap,Weyl bound)=[(10, 1, 138.9864, 124.0), (3, 1, 40.9665, 26.0), (1, 1, 12.9874, -2.0)]
PASS D4 hence in this model large W gaps all 16 Majoranas (both chirality blocks, both tastes): no zero mode, no light sector, so the 14W gap and large-W limit are statements about a trivially gapped phase, not about a chiral one
TOTAL: PASS=50 FAIL=0
HIT: scoped finite-algebra result (unrefereed, same family) for the nearest-neighbour staggered law with odd symbol: P_stag exchanges the two chirality blocks of the momentum fibre while Theta_M and the shifts preserve them, so {S_mu, P_stag, Theta_M} act transitively on the four chirality-by-taste blocks and a P_stag-invariant state has equal L and R spectral content; a chiral light block therefore needs P_stag broken (explicitly or spontaneously); not found in the sources read, which tested P_stag only as a mass-protecting symmetry
SUMMARY: Rebuilt from the lattice law, the fibre algebra shows P_stag flips chirality (Theta_M and shifts do not) and the symmetry group is transitive on the four chirality-by-taste blocks, so a chiral light block needs P_stag broken (explicitly or spontaneously); the carrier counts and the 14W eight-Majorana gap re-check exactly, and the large-W dimer gaps every mode, so it does not show a chiral phase. (runtime 71.0s)
